WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.730
Hey, guys.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.220
In this video we're going to talk about low
potassium.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.540
Why?

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.590
Because potassium is probably the number one
deficiency with most people, but it's the

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:12.630
hardest to detect.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:19.369
Because when you take a blood test, most of
the potassium, 98% of your potassium is inside

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:21.140
the cell, not outside the cell.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.560
So when they do a blood test, it's not going
to show up unless it's really, really, really

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.830
extreme.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.150
The type of testing you would have to do would
be an intracellular test.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.699
It's very sophisticated.

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:35.680
People don't really ask for it, doctors probably
don't even know about it, but there is a test

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.680
that you can do.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.120
But I like to go by symptoms.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.359
Here are some of the symptoms of low potassium.

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:43.190
And by the way, this is not Vitamin K.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.770
This is a chemical symbol of potassium.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.059
It's a K+.

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:50.649
When you're low potassium, the blood pressure
will increase.

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:51.649
Why?

00:00:51.649 --> 00:00:53.600
Because potassium is a physiological relaxer.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.870
It's a tranquilizer.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.700
It calms things down.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.090
Muscle cramps.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.570
Because potassium is an electrolyte.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.570
Sugar cravings.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.570
Why?

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.830
Because potassium helps you store sugar, and
it will actually help you get rid of sugar

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:15.950
cravings, because the storage of glucose needs
potassium.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.240
Constipation.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.540
Yeah.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.240
That's another symptom of low potassium.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.770
And then, high insulin.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.820
There's a relationship between sugar, blood
sugars, diabetes and potassium.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.750
In fact, when you have enough potassium, the
need for insulin goes down.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:39.190
So I always recommend potassium for diabetic
clients.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.190
This is another one.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.190
Muscle weakness.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.950
You could have this unexplainable muscle weakness
and not know why.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.950
Why?

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:49.610
Because the electrolytes are needed to help
the muscles contract.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.960
And that's why you have abnormal heartbeat.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.240
Because the heart is a muscle.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.540
Same thing with this muscle.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.770
Same thing with that muscles.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:05.670
These abnormal heartbeats, for example, like
atrial fibrillation, arrhythmias, that's a

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.899
combination of a deficiency of potassium and/or
magnesium.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:12.540
Anxiety.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.239
And sleeping problems, because potassium is
something to calm you down.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:21.849
If you're doing something that doesn't involve
a lot of � Like, some diet that doesn't

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:26.519
involve enough potassium, you can start manifesting
a lot of these symptoms.

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:30.510
Now, let's just go into what causes low potassium.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:37.030
Well, if you are sick and you vomit or, let's
say, you're a bulimic, that can cause that.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.480
Or maybe you're just not eating enough in
your diet.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.049
Now, you might say, "Well, I eat bananas."

00:02:42.049 --> 00:02:43.049
Right?

00:02:43.049 --> 00:02:48.439
Well, bananas only have 300 mg.

00:02:48.439 --> 00:02:57.950
You need 4,700 mg per day to hit your regular
amount that you need.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.709
You would have to consume 12 bananas, 11 bananas.

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:04.530
We don't want all that sugar.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:10.299
So what we want to do is we want to consume
our potassium from vegetables, from salad.

00:03:10.299 --> 00:03:12.879
And you're going to need about seven to 10
cups.

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:15.230
If you watch my other videos, I talk about
that.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.329
It's not that hard.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.540
You just have a couple big salads.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:22.780
If you don't like salad, take kale, maybe
a little bit of berry, blend it with water,

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.290
and drink your salad.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.700
That'll get the potassium in there.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.510
So we want to start to increase that.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.099
And that's how we increase it from the diet.

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:31.890
You're going to feel a lot better, too.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.909
Because if you're doing like an Atkins diet,
high protein, you're going to definitely need

00:03:36.909 --> 00:03:37.909
potassium.

00:03:37.909 --> 00:03:44.969
You're going to start feeling weakness, because
you don't have enough potassium.

00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:51.470
Ketosis is the state of fat-burning when you're
eating more fat, no carbs, and you can become

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:54.389
deficient in potassium from that, too.

00:03:54.389 --> 00:03:58.239
That's why they always modify the ketosis
diet, and I make sure that we have enough

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:02.359
greens and vegetables to help balance that.

00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:13.469
Also, potassium is necessary for the digestion
and breakdown and buildup of protein.

00:04:13.469 --> 00:04:17.950
People that are losing their hair, for example,
and they're eating just protein thinking that

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:22.280
they're going to get their hair back, without
potassium, sorry, it doesn't work.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.370
So we've got diuretics.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.730
Say, you're out of blood pressure medication.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:30.160
Well, you're going to deplete your potassium
and keep the blood pressure there.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.160
Interesting.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.980
That's the diuretic.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.300
That's one of the side effects.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:40.660
So you better make sure that your diuretic
is not pulling out potassium and you're not

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.190
putting it back in.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.190
High cortisol.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:45.440
That's stress.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.840
Stress can also deplete potassium.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:55.930
In fact, I've had people do advanced testing
on their potassium levels, and they are eating

00:04:55.930 --> 00:05:01.230
a tremendous amount of potassium, but because
they're under a tremendous amount of stress,

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.200
their potassium stays low.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.550
Because with the adrenal, it's almost like
you have a hole in the bucket and the potassium

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.530
goes right through.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:14.290
Again, when you're under stress, you need
even more potassium.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.320
Anyway, this potassium is really important.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.850
I forgot one.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:24.870
It's also high insulin will cause a low potassium,
and that's sugar.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.240
So let's just add that to the list.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:29.790
Consuming sugar will deplete your potassium.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.590
And you can even feel it in your heartbeat.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.880
It starts to go boom, boom, boom, boom, fast.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.390
A strong heartbeat, you can hear it in your
inner ear.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:42.740
That is a sign of low potassium because you
just ate a lot of sugar, and you need to start

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.560
consuming more salad to put that back.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.280
Last one is drinking too much water.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.200
This goes against what everyone says, that
you have to drink when you're � By the time

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.960
you drink, it's too late, because you don't
know when you're thirsty and � That's just

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:58.960
a myth.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:04.500
When you drink too much water, you create
a condition called hyponatremia, which is

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.770
a dilution of all your electrolytes, and then
your heart starts going out of balance and

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.130
you can have a heart attack by drinking too
much water.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:17.090
So you want to drink when you're thirsty so
you don't flush out all your electrolytes.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.550
Because you're drinking water, but you're
peeing out electrolytes.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.250
You're not putting in electrolytes.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:26.100
I like to hydrate my water with lemon, a little
bit of apple cider vinegar, maybe a little

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.400
Stevia if it's carbonated.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.670
I drink Pellegrino a lot or I drink filtered
water.

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:36.830
I just want to kind of give you an overall
on this very common deficiency that people

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.950
have and the symptoms so you can start thinking
with it.

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:44.280
And if you start having any of these, then
you know it could be connected with that,

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.990
and then you know the cause of that.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:47.990
Okay?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:48.990
I hope that helped.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.170
I will see you in the next video.

